The values here are invented — no real issue, user, organisation or token appears
in these files. Only the structure is borrowed.

## Which of these have been confirmed against a real Tracker

`every_fixture_still_has_the_shape_tracker_answers_with`, in `tests/live.rs`,
asks the real API once per endpoint and fails on a key a fixture claims and
Tracker no longer returns. Everything it can reach has been confirmed that way.

Seven cannot be reached, because no organisation available to us has any of the
thing they describe, and an empty array agrees with every fixture ever written:

    queue_fields.json        queue_versions.json    queue_local_fields.json
    components.json          issue_templates.json   all_sprints.json
    issue_remotelinks.json

Those are still only borrowed shapes. Treat a change to one of them as a change
to something nobody has checked — see issue #78, which is where the plan for
closing that gap lives.

`comments_html.json` is the exception in the other direction: it was recorded
from a real organisation, sanitised of names and ids, and is the evidence for
what `markupType` does (#77).
